From: mscharged-port
Subject: Read the banner captain's character class by member
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; same kind of fix as patch 0699.

StadiumWorldDrawable::UpdateModelMaterials picks the team banner texture.
When the task state is 0x10 or lower (gameplay, replay, NIS), it reads each
captain's character with a Wii byte offset: *(int*)((u8*)captain + 0x24).
R4QE01 has cmplwi 0x10 / ble, then lwz r30,0x24(r3) / lwz r29,0x24(r3) at
0x80279C50 / 0x80279C5C. That offset is
cCharacter::m_DetChar.m_eCharacterClass on the Wii.
Natively m_pSkinMesh starts at 0x10 and m_DetChar at 0x40. The read returns
the upper half of m_pSkinMesh[2], so the result is 0 (Mario's banners) when
that pointer is null or below 4 GiB, and an out-of-range GetCharacterInfo
index otherwise.

Stadium loading (TASK_FE_TO_GAME / TASK_BOOT_TO_GAME) takes the
GameInfoManager branch, but every StadiumWorldDrawable::Initialize clears
the cached banner again. WorldDrawable::DrawToView then calls
UpdateModelMaterials on each frame of a vertex-animated drawable, so the
first stadium intro frame (TASK_NIS) chooses the banner through this read.
On The Vice the hanging banners asked for mario/mario_banners, which is only
loaded when Mario plays, so they drew the missing-texture fallback
font/fixedWidthMedium (Wario vs Bowser run; Linux GCC build).

Natively the function reads the declared member. Wii builds are unchanged.
The member read also matches upstream: GC/3.0a5 with the R4QE01 flags gives
an identical .text for this TU (lwz 0x24(r3)).

diff --git a/src/Game/Render/StadiumWorldObjects.cpp b/src/Game/Render/StadiumWorldObjects.cpp
index f3c99fd..a83cbf6 100644
--- a/src/Game/Render/StadiumWorldObjects.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Render/StadiumWorldObjects.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,13 @@ static const char* sBannerProxyObjects[] = {
 // movement state, so it is read positionally until that layout is resolved.
 static inline int GetCaptainCharacter(cFielder* captain)
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    // Wii offset 0x24 is cCharacter::m_DetChar.m_eCharacterClass; natively
+    // it lands in m_pSkinMesh[2].
+    return captain->m_DetChar.m_eCharacterClass;
+#else
     return *(const int*)((const u8*)captain + 0x24);
+#endif
 }
 
 static unsigned long sStadiumBannerTexture;
